7. ev(g): Essential complexity, a refined measure of cyclomatic complexity emphasizing structured design.
8. b: Halstead’s program difficulty (an intermediate metric), which evaluates module intricacy in terms of operator-operand interactions.

These metrics encapsulate the complexity, logical structure, size, and cognitive effort of the software, all of which are predictive of software defects.
